     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 10,000 mg three times daily is 30 g a day. That is a toxic dose, not a matter of clinical preference. A single 10 g dose can cause acute liver failure in an adult, and repeating it three times a day would very likely cause severe liver injury or death. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't change that.\n\nYou can do either of these:\n\n- **If you meant 1,000 mg:** I can enter acetaminophen 1,000 mg by mouth three times daily (3 g/day) right away. Just tell me.\n- **If you believe there's a real reason for a very high dose:** Talk to your supervising resident, your attending, or pharmacy. I can't think of an indication for this dose. An attending or pharmacist can review it and place the order themselves if they think it's appropriate.\n\nIf the patient may have already taken a large amount of acetaminophen, that is an overdose. Contact your team and Poison Control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) right away. Don't treat it with a standing order.\n\nDo you want me to enter the 1,000 mg three times daily order?"
      }
     ],
